    "mantraNoteLi1": "Have a bowel movement and follow with a shower before sunrise.",
    "mantraNoteLi2": "Wearing clean clothing, sit facing east.",
    "mantraNoteLi3": "Play the mantra at a low volume.",
    "mantraNoteLi4": "Listen for forty consecutive days. After forty days you may chant along for an additional 40-day Chilla.",
    "mantraNoteLi5": "While chanting, breathe through the nose only — this supplies the purest prana to the mantra and enhances its effectiveness.",
    "mantraNoteLi6": "After the recording finishes, continue sitting quietly for a few minutes.",
    "mantraNoteP1": "Sri Shyamji Bhatnagar was a rare Nada Yogi — a master of the yoga of sound. The mantras offered here are not background music or casual listening. They carry potent subtle energy and should be approached with the same reverence one would bring to any sacred practice.",
    "mantraNoteP2": "The ideal time to listen is at or just before sunrise. To prepare:",
    "mantraNoteP3": "These sounds are to internalize the senses and should not be played for entertainment.",
    "mantraNoteP4": "If these prerequisites cannot be met initially, listen when your stomach is empty. Keep your eyes open and fixed downward at a single point.",
    "mantraNoteSubTitle": "Suggestions for Optimum Effects",
    "mantraNoteTitle": "A Note on These Mantras",
    "mantrasTitle": "Mantras",
