    "whatIsBody": "The Prana Calendar tracks which nostril should be dominant at sunrise each day based on the lunar cycle. Ancient Svar Yoga (breath) science shows that the nasal cycle mirrors the moon — and that the dominant nostril directly shifts brain hemisphere activity and body chemistry. The ionic charge of the surrounding atmosphere — which is shaped by lunar cycles, solar activity, ocean air, and environment — further influences which state the body is most receptive to. Synchronizing your breath with these rhythms supports health, clarity, and wellbeing. Check your nostril at sunrise, correct if needed, log your result, and over time build a map of your own natural rhythm.",
